{"ts":"2026-10-22T17:22:46.355488479Z","session":"837b52b4-d41d-4919-9e09-c68083ddd2a3","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"leader: claude\nworker: bwk\nevaluator: rsc\ntype: design\ninputs:\n  ticket: ethos-5y4r\nwrite_set:\n  - docs/design-opencode-plugin.md\n  - DESIGN.md\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - 'Answer every one of the 11 unresolved Copilot review threads on PR #536 that target docs/design-opencode-plugin.md (fetch them read-only with the gh api graphql reviewThreads query given in the context). For each thread, either amend the design so the finding no longer holds, or, if the finding is wrong, record why in the result evidence with a code/spec/doc citation (file:line). Each must be verified against real source (internal/, plugin/hooks/commit-msg.sh, docs/spec-opencode-integration.tex, .tmp/*.mdx/.ts OpenCode references, context7 for OpenCode) -- never accepted or rejected blind. The 11 cover: Effect-API registration shape; fixed ten-hop cap vs the spec ancestor-set guard; commit-msg.sh:55 skipping commit-trailers when MISSION_ID or DELEGATION_ID is set; resolve.SessionID accepting a nonempty ETHOS_SESSION naming a missing/dead session; ctx.session.list absence in the targeted release; snapshot-before-subscribe event-loss window; session create replacing (not idempotently registering) the roster; inherited parent ETHOS_SESSION in the shell env (two threads); WithDispatchPendingLock not making sidecar writes transactional and WriteCommitTrailers not taking the lock; ParentSession lineage missing when the live fork event was missed.'\n  - 'Apply the operator''s ruling on enablement (2026-10-22), replacing round 4''s usage-error behavior for bare `ethos enable` in Sec5 point 5 and DES-078 decision point 4: (a) `ethos enable` with no harness named, on an interactive terminal, prompts the user to choose which harness(es) to enable, listing every supported harness (claude, opencode) with BOTH preselected as the suggested default; (b) explicit forms `ethos enable 